      "writtenOn": "2026-07-30T12:03:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the suggestion.\n\nIt wasn\u0027t empty, but it had lost the useful parts: with just the whitelist change the object kept AddObject and Association.Definitions, but Name, Type and importantly Probe were gone. Agreed that\u0027s a regression for debugging.\n\nI think `Configuration.Platform` is the good way, so I\u0027ve done that in https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/92929. \n\nI didn\u0027t add a PDI definition for it, because Probe\u0027s signature isn\u0027t stable, and these properties were never in a PDI contract anyway. Happy to add one if you\u0027d prefer.",
      "parentUuid": "ac489468_3e3e2c68",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 44,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "5cab6267ccd873ae3ffcf6e1059fe9ed58990afe",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0a056fab_980d9733",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 48,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-30T16:36:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e What about Configuration.Probe as a way to have some interface to show Name, Probe and Type ?\n\nYes, ideally we\u0027d split those properties out into their own Configuration.Probe interface.  That\u0027d be a totally separate commit though.\n\n\u003e What would Configuration.Platform contain as properties?\n\nMaybe none?  Just knowing that it is a thing that exists is useful.\n\n\u003e But inventory decorators go on objects that have inventory interfaces, right?\n\nNot strictly, but typically, yes.  We also put it on firmwares I think when we do the probing to figure out what they are?",
      "parentUuid": "4b5f0e9e_9e0a423d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 44,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 55
