      "writtenOn": "2026-07-30T17:25:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e What did you mean by Probe\u0027s signature isn\u0027t stable?  Isn\u0027t it just a string?\n\nmaybe he meant that it can also be an array? \n\n```\n\"Probe\": {\n                    \"description\": \"The schema for an entity manager probe statement. Probes can be a single string or an array. Probes describe a match condition, for example when a DBus property has a specific value. When the match condition occurs, the information described by the Exposes property is exported onto the DBus.\",\n                    \"anyOf\": [\n                        {\n                            \"type\": \"string\"\n                        },\n                        {\n                            \"type\": \"array\",\n                            \"items\": {\n                                \"type\": \"string\"\n                            },\n                            \"minItems\": 1\n                        }\n                    ]\n                },\n```\n\nI don\u0027t think this is a blocker though. We could just force it to be \u0027array of string\u0027 in all cases even if there is only a string as probe.",
